- **Boundary:** Markup attributes
  - **What to validate:** `id` (stable element id)
  - **How (stack-specific):** Besides CSS matching and `getElementById`, a Dioxus document's `element_id` / `element_ids` read the HTML `id` as an element's author key only when it is non-empty, contains no `/` and is the first element in document pre-order to claim it; an empty, `/`-bearing or later-duplicate value gives no key and anchors nothing; an element with no key reads one of three `/`-bearing paths — an anchored path `{key}//{segment}` (then `/{segment}` per further DOM level) under the nearest element of its own component instance that reads an author key, else its component path, else its document path, a template root owned by another component instance restarting at that component's chain, so an anchor acts inside one component only; an author key holds no `/`, an anchored path is the only id holding `//`, and a component or document path has no empty segment, so no `id` can make two ids equal — a key spelled like a component name included (`Item//b:0` beside `Item/b:0`) — the anchored tier ratified by the founder (2026-10-06); a non-element, stale or detached node reads `None`, and no path panics; the id is computed on demand and escher's own code writes it to no log, DOM or vdom — an author-key id is the element's HTML `id`, though, which Stylo's own records carry (`style::*`, `selectors::matching`): those targets are outside the sink's allowlist, so since 2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist a host that installs escher's sink drops them whole and prints that value at no `RUST_LOG` level
 — the instrument's id needles found on stderr, before → after the drop: the `escher-session` binary on `crud` 15 of 15 → 0 at `debug` and at `trace`, the windowed `seven_guis_native` on Home 11 of 11 → 0 at `debug` and at `trace`, and 0 on both at the default level and at `info` before and after (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/evidence/by-level.md); under the `accessibility` feature `DioxusDocument::accessibility_tree` carries it as each element node's AccessKit `author_id` — never on a `TextRun`, the document root or the synthetic `Window` node, and never by indexing the slab with a tree id — so it leaves the process only through the platform accessibility adapter when an assistive technology is active, the crossing text runs and labels already take (ratified by the operator, 2026-10-06); since 2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff the adapter receives the tree on change as well as on its initial request — on a poll that reported work the windowed shell's `View::poll` takes the document's changed set (`BaseDocument::take_changed_nodes`) and, under `accessibility`, rebuilds the platform tree when the set it took was non-empty, where before that chunk the poll-time refresh did not run and the tree was built once — the same crossing and the same content classes (ids as `author_id`, accessible names), more often (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07; its windowed witness is still owed — no windowed run witnesses the refresh on the dev host); since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions the tree that crossing is handed is asserted headlessly on the stand in both layout modes
 — `Document::accessibility_tree` called through `&dyn blitz_dom::Document`, as `AccessibilityState::update_tree` calls it, equals the document's own `accessibility_tree()` node for node with the same focus and root, every `author_id` on it is its node's `DioxusDocument::element_id`, none empty, all digits or holding `0x`, and each lean task's tree carries at least its controls' ids — and the refresh's two halves are proven there too: after a drained changed set a Tab and an Enter each leave `has_changes()` true and that tree reads the new focus and the rewritten name (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:310-352; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:363-410 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions/report.md); what the platform adapter hands an assistive technology stays unread — the stand builds no adapter, kept so on the founder's F1 «Пока нет, перенести (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-14, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer as his chosen option label, inputs#I2 of escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions), that witness owned by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line that reads `re-carried:0.2.0`, at an active assistive technology this version does not reach; since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states the crossing carries a third content class, control states — `selected`, `toggled` and `invalid` on each element node whose markup states them, closed enums and booleans, never an attribute's value as typed (`toggled` from `aria-checked` on a checkable role and from `aria-pressed` on every other; the `aria-selected` · `aria-pressed` · `aria-checked` · `aria-invalid` row) — a widening ratified by the founder (2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Ратифицировать»;
 the English wording is the overseer's), its windowed witness owed like the refresh's: no check reads the three at the adapter on the dev host; since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync the names it carries include `aria-labelledby`'s computed text (the `aria-label` · `<label for>` row), and it carries a fourth content class, descriptions — `aria-description`'s own text and `aria-describedby`'s targets as `described_by` (the `aria-describedby` · `aria-description` row) — a widening by upstream merge ratified as upstream's behaviour by the founder (2026-10-17, «Утвердить оба (Рекомендую)», both sources confirmed by his «Подтвердить все 10 (Рекомендую)», 2026-10-18), its windowed witness owed like the states'; under the same feature `DioxusDocument::snapshot` is a second, in-process reader of that `author_id` — it takes no argument, copies the id verbatim into `SnapshotNode.id`, resolves each tree id through `BaseDocument::get_node` (never an index) and omits a node that does not resolve — and adds no crossing of its own: the snapshot has one text form, `Snapshot::to_text` (same feature; no JSON form, no `Display` impl, no parser of the text), which writes each node's id as a quoted `id=` field in `str`'s `Debug` form, so the field never holds a line break or a bare `"`; that text was returned to its caller only until 2026-10-10-driver-cli (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07) and no log or event carries the snapshot or its text — the one file that does is a kept check: since 2026-10-19-session-recording a recorded session's calls, the ids they named among them, and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay each answer kept whole, a `snapshot`'s text and every diff included, a shot's pixels excepted, owner-only and never logged but for the two committed stand checks in git (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19: F3 B, F1 A);
 since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the driver's `snapshot` command returns it through `Session::run` to the code that called `run` — `to_text`'s one caller outside the tests — and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli that caller can be a session host: a hosted `snapshot`'s answer carries the text, ids included, over the session socket (`ok v3 accepted <json>`) and onto the `escher-session` client's stdout as one line of JSON, the in-process text unchanged (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Сокет несёт команды», the English wording is the overseer's; the operator's 2026-10-07 answer that nothing of it goes on the socket is superseded) — so escher's own code now gives the id three exits — and, since 2026-10-19-session-recording, a fourth at rest, a kept check holding the ids a recorded session's calls named and, since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay, every id its kept answers read — owner-only, and in the two committed Counter checks under `tests/blitz-tests/checks/` in git (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19) — the platform adapter, the driver's answers and, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, MCP tool results on the `escher-session mcp` role's stdout — an accepted `snapshot` the screen text itself — a paged one its JSON line `{"text","part","parts"}` holding the same text —, any other accepted call its JSON line (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, «Ратифицировать как есть», relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label; the English wording is the overseer's) — and an id a call names arrives also as an MCP tool's string `id` argument, bounded by `validate` inside `Session::run`; neither the id nor the snapshot carries a `NodeId`, `ElementId`, `ScopeId` or pointer; under the same feature `DioxusDocument::unkeyed_actionable` is a third in-process reader of the id
 — it takes no argument, takes ids from `element_ids()` and roles from `accessibility_tree`, resolves each node through `BaseDocument::get_node` and skips one that does not resolve, logs nothing and never panics, and returns an `UnkeyedActionable` (`node`, `id`, `tag`, `role`, `focusable`, `interactive_role`, `listener`) for each actionable element whose id holds a `/`; an entry holds the id, tag and role and never the element's text content, accessible name or an attribute value of that element, and its `node` field is a process-local `NodeId`, meaningful in process only; it adds no crossing of its own — no wire form, no log, event, socket or file, and no driver, CLI or MCP command yet (whether it becomes one is owned by a route entry) — the id's exits being the platform adapter, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli the driver's answers, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface MCP tool results and, since 2026-10-19-session-recording, a kept check's call targets and, since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay, its kept answers' ids; under the same feature `Snapshot::diff` is a fourth in-process reader of the id, through the snapshot model only — a pure function of two `Snapshot` values (no document access, no failure path, no log, no print) that copies ids into `DiffNode.id`, `DiffNode.parent` and `SnapshotDiff.removed`, holds no `NodeId`, `ElementId`, `ScopeId`, AccessKit id or pointer, and has no text form, `Display` impl, JSON form or parser of its own; since 2026-10-19-visual-lint escher-driver's `Session::lint` is a fifth reader of the id — it takes no argument, reads the snapshot and returns `Finding`s holding ids, closed defect words and numbers only (no `NodeId`, page text, colour or control value; a text control's value never measured), and crosses as the `lint` verb's answer (`Command::Lint` → `Outcome::Linted`, written `{"findings":[…]}`) on every ratified carrier
 — the socket's `call`, the command line, MCP and a kept check, kept whole — a ratified boundary widening, with no log site, print, span or field carrying a finding (its `command` span `verb` and, refused, `cause` only) and `VERBS` holding twelve; until 2026-10-10-driver-cli a diff was returned to its caller only (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07, with the snapshot text's answer), and since that chunk the driver's `Outcome::to_json` writes a returned diff as JSON — a node keyed by the schema's node fields in order — and an acting command's answer carries it over the session socket and onto the client's stdout (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Сокет несёт команды»; the English wording is the overseer's); no log or event carries a diff, and since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay a file only as a kept check's kept answer, owner-only and never logged, the two committed stand checks in git the one exception (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19: F3 B, F1 A) — while, since 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans, the three list lengths of a diff the driver returns (`added` · `removed` · `changed`: counts only, no node, id, name or value) are recorded on the driver's command span, which escher's sink prints at `info` or below (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-09: the sentence stands, and it gains the clarification that a diff's content never reaches a log while its three sizes — the counts of added, removed and changed — may; the Driver command schema row; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md); since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the driver's five acting commands — `click`, `type`, `press`, `advance` and, since 2026-10-07-refusal-detection, `scroll` — return the diff of their one settled step through `Session::run` to the code that called `run` — `diff`'s one caller outside the tests
 — in process (the operator, 2026-10-07, at that chunk's plan forks) or, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, as a hosted call's JSON answer over the session socket and on the command line's stdout and, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, as an accepted MCP tool call's result on the `mcp` role's stdout (the ratified crossing, above); a keyed list row's segment carries its Dioxus key (`{tag}[{key}]`), and a Dioxus key that is empty or holds `/` is refused — the row reads the positional `{tag}:{n}` segment instead (`/ul:0/li:1` beside `/ul:0/li[ok]`), each of the two cases witnessed by a unit test; the 7GUIs CRUD row also carries the HTML `id` `crud-person-{person.id}`, so its stable id is that author key, built like its Dioxus key from its person's model-assigned `u64` (fixture `crud-person-0..2`, Create from `crud-person-3`), and Home's seven cards read the fixed-slug author keys `task-card-{slug}` — never a list index, pointer, hash, clock or process-local value — so a row reads the same id across a re-render, a remount and a second process, and a dropped pre-remount `NodeId` reads `None` with no panic; since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the id also has its first consumer that takes one IN: the driver's `click`, `type` and — since 2026-10-07-refusal-detection — `scroll`, through `Session::run`, take a caller-supplied id — already bounded at 1 to 1024 bytes by `validate` — and look it up on the screen as it reads now: the id names an element when the screen's snapshot lists it and the first pair of `element_ids()` whose id equals it, found by a linear search, has a node that resolves through `get_node`, never by index; otherwise the call is refused with nothing run and no panic — `stale` when the session's record holds the id, `not-found` when it does not;
 the lookup is made anew on every call and the session keeps no `NodeId` between calls, but since that chunk the session is itself a holder of the id: a record of the ids its screens have read, kept to tell those two causes apart — id text only, in a crate-private structure behind one private field, at most 4096 ids with the one read longest ago forgotten first, empty at `Session::start` and living as long as the session, read by no public item, written to no log, event, socket or file, and fed only from snapshots the session itself takes — once `validate` has admitted a call, and, since 2026-10-19-visual-lint, on `Session::lint`, which takes no argument (the operator, 2026-10-07, at that chunk's plan forks); the bound counts ids, not bytes — the ids recorded are the app's own element ids, which `validate` never sees, so one longer than 1024 bytes can be named by no call, and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli it is not recorded: the record holds at most 4096 ids of at most 1024 bytes each (the operator, 2026-10-10, at that chunk's plan forks; held by the unit test `the_record_holds_no_id_longer_than_a_call_can_name`); no field of `Session`, `Outcome` or `Refusal` holds a `NodeId`, and no `NodeId` crosses; the record stays in process, while the id a call names now comes from outside it — the `--id` flag of the `escher-session` command line and a percent-escaped text value of the socket's `call` request — and passes `validate`'s 1 to 1024 byte bound on each side, in the client before a session is touched and in the host inside `Session::run` (until that chunk a call was built and run in one process: the operator, 2026-10-07, at the act-by-id chunk's plan forks) (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:186-282; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:337-361; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:397-441; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:443-594;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:257-290; examples/seven_guis/src/tasks/crud.rs:92-108; examples/seven_guis/src/app.rs:144; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_persistence.rs:1-3; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:96-115; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:130-195; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot.rs:1-5; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot_text.rs:53; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_text.rs:1-7; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/actionable.rs:15-44; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/actionable.rs:55-89; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:1-4; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:376-382; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot_diff.rs:108; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_diff.rs:1-12; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document_tests.rs:48-78; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:188-204; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:503-520; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:380-425; packages/escher-driver/src/session.rs:66-117; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_ids.rs:1-15; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_refused.rs:1-9) — the refresh on change and the diff as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md, the refused Dioxus key's two witnesses at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-audit-corrections/report.md, the id as a driver argument and the driver's returns at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/report.md, the session's record and the `stale` answer at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md

- **Boundary:** Markup attributes
  - **What to validate:** `input type="range"` — `min` · `max` · `step` · `value`, and its default actions (keys, pointerdown, click)
  - **How (stack-specific):** Since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, in every document — the browser app's remote pages included — an `input` whose `type` reads `range` (ASCII case-insensitive) holds a current value apart from its `value` attribute (`RangeInputData`, an `f64`), and the markup and the user's keys and pointer move it within bounds: the four attributes are read through `parse_float`, the HTML rules for parsing floating-point number values, a parse error, NaN or an infinity reading as absent and `-0` as `0` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:232-270; its private steps `take_sign`, `take_digits` and `take_exponent` since 2026-10-16-handler-splits-and-readme, the readings unchanged, packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:272-301); `min` defaults to 0 and `max` to 100, a `max` below `min` reading as `min`; `step` defaults to 1, a step ≤ 0 or unparsable reading 1 and `any` setting no grid and stepping by 1 on a key; the step base is `min` where it parses, else the `value` attribute, else 0; the default value is the midpoint, computed `min/2 + max/2` so it cannot overflow; every seed, attribute write and move is sanitized — clamped to `[min, max]`, moved to the nearest grid value, the greater on a tie, the grid index computed `value/step − base/step` so the difference of two finite bounds cannot overflow, then rounded to the decimals of the step and the base and written in its shortest round-trip form (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:67-75; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:85-206) — so the value stays finite, bounded and on its grid on degenerate markup (an 8-row unit table, packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:471-507, and 7 integration rows in both layout modes, tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:181-222);
 the default actions: on a focused range input with no `disabled` attribute (presence) a pressed `ArrowRight` or `ArrowUp` steps up, `ArrowLeft` or `ArrowDown` steps down, `Home` and `End` go to the minimum and the maximum, and every other key does nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:102-107; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:146-163); a main-button pointerdown, its arm after the `disabled` arm, sets the value from the hit's fraction of the content box, clamped to `[0, 1]`, a content box of no width reading 0 (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:449-453; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:650-661; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:509-511; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:663-678); a click, after the `disabled` check, focuses it and changes no value (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:765-777); every change goes through one path that marks the changed set and fires one `input` event carrying the formatted value, a move that changes nothing firing none (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:333-354); a disabled range takes neither key nor click (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:240-262); a `value` write re-seeds the current value and a `min`, `max` or `step` write or removal re-sanitizes it — a departure from the spec's dirty-value flag, the cost the founder's first fork answer took on (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:361-367; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:388-390; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:525-532); the rules module holds no print, log site, `unwrap`, `expect`, panic or env read outside its tests, and the chunk's added engine lines none either (the gate censuses read 0);
 the current value leaves only as form submission's entry (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:334-335), the `input` event's value and the snapshot's `NodeState.value` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:252-255) — a control value, crossing the driver's answers and MCP results inside the ratified carriers, with no carrier, verb, field, log field or span added — and no accessibility node value or action changes — an engine change for every document and a boundary widening, ratified by the founder: his ruling of 2026-10-07 «Пусть будет а», his answers to the three forks of 2026-10-13 «Отдельное текущее значение», «Стрелки + Home/End (Рекомендую)» and «Клик даёт фокус (Рекомендую)», and his confirm of the wrap's answer card the same day «Подтвердить (Рекомендую)», which also covers the three consequences the operator confirmed at the review — each by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label, the English wording the overseer's — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-range-input-interaction/report.md
